[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `run_all.sh` runs the full suite against.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axis 2 — public entry points (complete, lowest level first)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Taken from the `extern` declarations in `mdmacros.h:40-42, 104-110` and from
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `nm -D` on the C `.so` — **not** just the convenience wrappers.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | level | entry point | composition |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-------|-------------|-------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | leaf  | `op_add(int,int)` | `a + b`; contains no macro → identical in all 24 configs |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | leaf  | `op_sub(int,int)` | `a - b`; ditto |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | leaf  | `op_mul(int,int)` | `a * b`; ditto |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | data  | `G_OP` | mutable `int (*)(int,int)` object initialised to `OP_FN(OP)`; depends on **OP** |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | data  | `G_OP_NAME` | mutable `const char *` object initialised to `STR(OP)`; depends on **OP** |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | mid   | `helper_ptr(int,int)` | `OP_FN(OP)` through a local fn pointer + `printf`; depends on **OP** |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | mid   | `use_generated(int n)` | `accum_<OP>(n)` = `INIT_FOR(OP)` + `DISPATCH_REP` `switch (n)` + `printf`; depends on **OP** and on **n**, *not* on REPEAT |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | high  | `helper_call(int,int)` | `OP_FN(OP)(a,b)` **and** `RUN_LOOP(OP, acc, REPEAT)` + `printf`, returns `r + acc`; depends on **OP × REPEAT** |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | top   | `main(argc, argv)` | `atoi` ×2, `OP_FN(OP)`, `RUN_LOOP(…, REPEAT)`, `helper_call`, `helper_ptr`, `use_generated(REPEAT)`, `G_OP`, `G_OP_NAME`, 2 `printf`s; depends on **OP × REPEAT** and on the argv shapes |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axis 3 — input shapes the code distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | shape class | values | why the C distinguishes it |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-------------|--------|----------------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `int` pair for `op_*` / `helper_*` | `0`, `±1`, `±2`, `±7`, `INT_MAX`, `INT_MAX-1`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN+1`, `65535`, `65536`, `-65536`, `46340`, `46341`, `-46341` (17 boundary values, full 17×17 cross-product) plus randomized values | the bodies are branch-free but *value dependent*: `46340²` is the last non-overflowing square, `46341²` the first overflowing one; `INT_MIN * -1` and `INT_MIN - 1` are the wrap pivots |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `n` for `use_generated` | `0,1,2,3,4,5,6` — seven distinct `case` arms (h:84-90) | each arm unrolls a different number of `STEP_OP`s |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `n` for `use_generated` | anything else → `default:` (h:91) | see `ERRORS.md` E-02..E-07 |
